  "worked_solution": "Here, we have the product of two functions $u(x)={x}^{3}$ and $v(x)={e}^{x}.$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{\u2032}(x) & =({x}^{3})^{\u2032}{e}^{x}+{x}^{3}({e}^{x})^{\u2032} \\\\  & =(3{x}^{2})({e}^{x})+({x}^{3})({e}^{x}) \\\\  & =3{x}^{2}{e}^{x}+{x}^{3}{e}^{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
